<title>USA: South Korea buys 23,300 T U.S. wheat - exporters.</title>
<headline>South Korea buys 23,300 T U.S. wheat - exporters.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two South Korean flour mills, Cheil and Dong Ah, bought a total of 23,300 tonnes of U.S. wheat overnight for November 20-December 20 shipment from the Pacific Northwest, U.S. exporters said.</p>
<p>They bought 10,500 tonnes of soft white wheat, 7,300 of hard red winter and 5,500 of spring wheat.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
</text>
